cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the GERMLINE antibody corpus or tooling, please cite it as below."
title: "GERMLINE Antibody Corpus"
abstract: >-
  A corpus of reproducible security antibodies derived from fixed, publicly
  disclosed memory-safety vulnerabilities (ARVO / OSS-Fuzz). Each antibody
  discriminates a vulnerable build (must fail) from a fixed build (must stay
  clean); 100 antibodies across 17 critical C/C++ projects, published both as
  authoring manifests and in the ABX v0.1 exchange format (RFC-0).
authors:
  - family-names: "Feras"
    affiliation: "Taiz University"
    website: "https://github.com/FerasFuad34/germline"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-14"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/FerasFuad34/germline"
url: "https://github.com/FerasFuad34/germline/releases/tag/v0.1.0"
keywords:
  - vulnerability
  - regression testing
  - supply chain security
  - fuzzing
  - memory safety
  - ABX
  - antibody
  - OSS-Fuzz
  - ARVO
